# Reviewer Design

## Role
Judge interface output against the project's own design system: its design tokens, component and layout rules, motion rules, and quality bars.

## Inputs
- design system (tokens, rules, quality bars from design/DESIGN.md and design/tokens.json)
- interface output (HTML, React components, CSS, user-facing pages, or other interface artifacts)

## Outputs
- review (JSON format with verdict and findings)

## Rules
- Work only from the inputs listed above and the work order in the packet.
- If the project has no design system (no design/DESIGN.md), your verdict MUST be `changes_requested` with a finding stating that no design system exists for the project.
- If the project has a design system, review the interface output against:
  - Design tokens: Are the correct colors, typography, spacing values being used?
  - Component and layout rules: Do components follow the documented patterns?
  - Motion rules: Does any animation or transition follow the motion guidelines?
  - Quality bars: Does the interface meet the stated quality bars for visual hierarchy, scale contrast, spacing rhythm, and responsive behavior?
- Focus on the design system the project has defined. Do not impose external design opinions or preferences that are not documented in the project's design system.
- A design token marked as "TODO" or placeholder means the project hasn't defined that value yet. Flag missing values as findings only if the interface output actually uses undefined tokens.
- Findings should be specific and actionable: cite which quality bar was violated, which token was used incorrectly, or which rule was not followed.
- Your verdict must be one of: `approved`, `changes_requested`, or `comment`.
- Produce the output as a JSON object, not as chat text.

## Output Format

Return a JSON object with this structure:

```json
{
  "station": "reviewer-design",
  "verdict": "approved | changes_requested | comment",
  "findings": [
    "Specific finding with reference to design system rule or quality bar",
    "Another finding if applicable"
  ]
}
```

## Examples

### Example 1: No design system exists
```json
{
  "station": "reviewer-design",
  "verdict": "changes_requested",
  "findings": [
    "No design system exists for this project. The project must define design/DESIGN.md and design/tokens.json before interface output can be reviewed against design standards."
  ]
}
```

### Example 2: Interface violates quality bar
```json
{
  "station": "reviewer-design",
  "verdict": "changes_requested",
  "findings": [
    "Quality bar violation: Scale Contrast - The button text has only 2.8:1 contrast ratio against its background, failing the minimum 4.5:1 requirement stated in the quality bars.",
    "Token usage: The page uses hardcoded color '#FF5733' instead of the defined primary color token."
  ]
}
```

### Example 3: Interface meets design system
```json
{
  "station": "reviewer-design",
  "verdict": "approved",
  "findings": []
}
```


---

## Task packet: reviewer-design (benchmark arm)

Work order: benchmark the design station models (GitHub issue 22 in arananet/anvil-factory). Judge the interface output below against the project's design system. The design system, the interface output and the rendered evidence follow in this packet. There is no other material: work only from what is in this packet and the attached capture.

## Design system

### design/DESIGN.md

# Meridian Patch Design System

## Color Palette

The Meridian Patch uses a refined, nature-inspired palette:

- **paper** `#FAFAF6` - Page background
- **ink** `#14201B` - Headings and primary text
- **pine** `#53685C` - Secondary text and captions
- **teal** `#0E7C66` - Primary action background
- **coral** `#FF6B4A` - Reserved exclusively for the price badge
- **line** `#E3E6DF` - Borders and dividers

## Typography

### Type Scale

All text sizes are drawn from this scale (in px): 12, 14, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 56, 64.

- Hero titles must use at least 56px
- Body text must use at least 16px

### Font Stacks

- **Headings**: The first family in every heading stack is "Space Grotesk"
- **Body**: The first family in the body stack is "Inter"

### Line Heights

- **Headings**: 1.2 (unitless)
- **Body text**: 1.5 (unitless)

## Spacing

All margin and padding values are multiples of 8. Zero is permitted.

## Border Radius

Radius tokens (in px): 4, 8, 12, 16, 999.

All border-radius values must use one of these tokens.

## Focus States

Links and buttons show a `:focus-visible` outline with these properties:
- 2px solid teal (`#0E7C66`)
- 2px offset

## Accessibility

### Contrast

Text on the paper background must meet at least 4.5:1 contrast ratio by the WCAG relative luminance formula.

### Motion

Transitions are permitted only when accompanied by a `prefers-reduced-motion` media query block that disables them for users who prefer reduced motion.

## Quality Bars

### Color Usage
- [ ] All colors are from the documented palette
- [ ] Coral is used only on the price badge
- [ ] Text contrast on paper meets 4.5:1 minimum

### Typography
- [ ] Hero titles are at least 56px from the type scale
- [ ] Body text is at least 16px from the type scale
- [ ] All font sizes are from the type scale
- [ ] Headings use Space Grotesk as first family
- [ ] Body text uses Inter as first family
- [ ] Heading line height is 1.2
- [ ] Body line height is 1.5

### Spacing
- [ ] All margins and paddings are multiples of 8

### Border Radius
- [ ] All border-radius values use documented radius tokens

### Focus and Accessibility
- [ ] Focus-visible outline is 2px solid teal with 2px offset
- [ ] Transitions have prefers-reduced-motion block


### design/tokens.json

```json
{
  "colors": {
    "paper": "#FAFAF6",
    "ink": "#14201B",
    "pine": "#53685C",
    "teal": "#0E7C66",
    "coral": "#FF6B4A",
    "line": "#E3E6DF"
  },
  "type_scale": [12, 14, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 56, 64],
  "spacing_rhythm": 8,
  "radius": [4, 8, 12, 16, 999],
  "line_heights": {
    "headings": 1.2,
    "body": 1.5
  },
  "fonts": {
    "heading": "Space Grotesk",
    "body": "Inter"
  }
}

```

## Interface output

### src/page.html

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Meridian Patch - Revolutionary Health Technology</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
            background: #FAFAF6;
            color: #14201B;
        }

        #page {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 64px 32px;
        }

        #hero-title {
            font-family: "Space Grotesk", sans-serif;
            font-size: 48px;
            line-height: 1.2;
            color: #14201B;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        #hero-sub {
            font-size: 20px;
            line-height: 1.5;
            color: #5C6F66;
            margin-bottom: 32px;
        }

        #cta-primary {
            background: #0E7C66;
            color: #FAFAF6;
            padding: 16px 32px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            border: none;
            font-size: 16px;
            font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: opacity 0.2s;
            margin-right: 16px;
        }

        #cta-primary:hover {
            opacity: 0.9;
        }

        #price-badge {
            background: #FF6B4A;
            color: #FAFAF6;
            padding: 8px 16px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            font-size: 14px;
            font-weight: 600;
            display: inline-block;
        }

        #section {
            padding-top: 30px;
            padding-bottom: 64px;
        }

        #heading-2 {
            font-family: "Arial", sans-serif;
            font-size: 32px;
            line-height: 1.2;
            color: #14201B;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        #body-text {
            font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
            font-size: 15px;
            line-height: 1.33;
            color: #14201B;
            margin-bottom: 24px;
        }

        #caption {
            font-size: 12px;
            line-height: 1.5;
            color: #E3E6DF;
            margin-bottom: 16px;
        }

        #link-inline {
            color: #FF6B4A;
            text-decoration: underline;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        #card {
            background: #FAFAF6;
            border: 1px solid #E3E6DF;
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 24px;
            margin-top: 32px;
        }

        @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            * {
                transition: none !important;
                animation: none !important;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="page">
        <header>
            <h1 id="hero-title">Transform Your Health with Meridian Patch</h1>
            <p id="hero-sub">Advanced biosensor technology meets elegant design</p>
            <button id="cta-primary">Start Your Journey</button>
            <span id="price-badge">$199</span>
        </header>

        <section id="section">
            <h2 id="heading-2">Why Meridian Patch?</h2>
            <p id="body-text">The Meridian Patch combines cutting-edge health monitoring with seamless daily wear. Our proprietary biosensor array tracks your vital signs in real-time, providing actionable insights through our companion app. Designed for comfort and accuracy, the Meridian Patch represents the future of personal health technology.</p>
            <p id="caption">Clinical validation pending FDA review</p>
            <a href="#" id="link-inline">Learn more about our technology</a>

            <div id="card">
                <h3 style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; color: #14201B; margin-bottom: 16px;">What's Included</h3>
                <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
                    <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; color: #14201B; margin-bottom: 8px;">30-day supply of Meridian Patches</li>
                    <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; color: #14201B; margin-bottom: 8px;">Premium companion app access</li>
                    <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; color: #14201B; margin-bottom: 8px;">24/7 health insights dashboard</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</body>
</html>

```

## Rendered evidence

One rendered capture of the page (full page, 1280 px wide) is attached to this message as an image. Judge the page against the design system above, using both the source and the capture.


## Output contract

Answer with a single JSON object and nothing else, in exactly this shape:
{"station": "<your station id>", "verdict": "pass", "findings": ["..."]}
The verdict must be one of: pass, fail, changes_requested. Findings must be concrete and checkable against the spec, the code and the tests.
